events.body:
I added an optional `coinbase` argument to `makeTemplate()`. Based on my draft JDS implementation https://github.com/stratum-mining/sv2-apps/pull/599 this does appear useful, e.g. for checking the reward amount. We still generate a dummy if no coinbase transaction is provided.

@ismaelsadeeq `collectTxs()` is the constructor so it needs to return an interface. I don't think it can return both the `TxCollection` interface _and_ the list of missing transactions. But clients [can chain requests](https://capnproto.org/rpc.html) (not sure if we've fully implemented the on the libmultiprocess side).

I can also imagine a (slight) benefit in clients being able to call `unknownTxPos()` multiple times, e.g. maybe in a future upgrade we could have the node request missing transactions from peers - not sure how useful that is though.

